    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0083" n="817" xml:id="pg817"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Terres.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 153, of the 9th
                    ultimo, reporting that the attachment levied by Mr. Devot on the second
                    installment of the indemnity due to Mr. Richard Allen had been raised and the
                    amount paid over to your legation.</p>
                <p>The Department is glad to learn that the matter was amicably arranged.</p>
                <p>Your communication to the Haitian secretary of foreign affairs of the views of
                    this Government in regard to the matter was, however, timely, and will doubtless
                    tend to a better understanding of the subject in the future. You should,
                    however, have sent a copy of your communication.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
